.TH CHOOM 1 "2026-06-14" "choom 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
choom \- minimal SSH terminal sharing relay
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B choom server
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B choom host
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ command ]
.br
.B choom clients
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B choom
shares a terminal over SSH. A
.B host
runs its local shell and forwards it through a central
.B relay
(\fBchoom server\fR); viewers connect with a plain
.BR ssh (1)
using a token as the username \(em read-only or read-write. An optional read-only
browser view and asciicast recording are available. The shell runs on the host; the
relay only forwards bytes and never executes code.
.PP
There is no end-to-end encryption: a relay operator can read and inject into hosted
sessions. Only host on a relay you trust.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B server
Run the relay. Generates an Ed25519 host key on first start. Hosts authenticate by
public key (\fBauthorized_keys\fR or the built-in default key); viewers authenticate
by token.
.TP
.B host
Share the local shell ($SHELL by default, or \fIcommand\fR). Prints a read-only and
a read-write link.
.TP
.B clients
List the active viewers of your own session.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Common
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Load options from a YAML file. Keys are the long option names; explicit flags
override the file.
.SS server
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-listen\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Port to listen on (default 2200).
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-host " " \fINAME\fR
Hostname advertised to viewers in the links.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-web " " \fISPEC\fR
Enable the web view, e.g. \fB0.0.0.0:8080\fR. Empty disables it.
.TP
.BR \-W ", " \-\-web\-url " " \fIURL\fR
Public base URL advertised for the web view (e.g. behind a TLS gateway).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-record " " \fIDIR\fR
Enable recording storage; hosts opt in per session with \fBchoom host \-\-record\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-record\-all
Record every session, even without the host opting in.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-default\-key
Do not trust the built-in default key (private relay).
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-authorized\-keys " " \fIPATH\fR
File of public keys allowed to host.
.TP
.B \-\-max\-sessions \fIN\fR
Global cap on concurrent sessions (default 200; 0 = unlimited).
.TP
.B \-\-max\-viewers \fIN\fR
Cap on viewers per session (default 50; 0 = unlimited).
.TP
.B \-\-rate\-limit \fIN\fR
New connections per source IP per minute (default 60; 0 = off).
.TP
.B \-\-record\-max\-age\-days \fIN\fR, \-\-record\-max\-mb \fIN\fR
Recording retention by age (default 7) and total size (default 500).
.TP
.B \-\-downloads \fIDIR\fR
Directory of prebuilt binaries served at \fB/download/\fR.
.SS host
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-server " " \fINAME\fR
Relay to connect to (default choom.this-is-fine.io).
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-identity " " \fIKEY\fR
Private SSH key (else the bundled default key).
.TP
.B \-\-record
Ask the relay to record this session.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The container entrypoint maps \fBCHOOM_*\fR variables to the server options above
(\fBCHOOM_HOSTNAME\fR, \fBCHOOM_WEB\fR, \fBCHOOM_RECORD\fR, \fBCHOOM_MAX_SESSIONS\fR,
\fBCHOOM_RATE_LIMIT\fR, \fBCHOOM_RECORD_ALL\fR, ...). See the README.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I host_key
Relay Ed25519 host key (generated, mode 0600).
.TP
.I authorized_keys
Public keys allowed to host.
.TP
.I *.cast
asciicast v2 recordings (mode 0600), downloadable at \fB/s/<ro-token>/cast\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Public host (uses the default server and key):
.PP
.RS
.EX
choom host
.EE
.RE
.PP
Private relay:
.PP
.RS
.EX
choom server \-\-no\-default\-key \-a authorized_keys \-w 0.0.0.0:8080
choom host \-s relay.example \-i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 \-\-no\-default\-key
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR asciinema (1)
